      eslint 8→10 + typescript-eslint 6→8 (flat config only — root
      eslint.config.mjs, legacy .eslintrc deleted, eslint-plugin docs updated).
      typescript ~5.9.3→6.0.3 (tsconfig modernization: NodeNext module/resolution,
      explicit per-package rootDir, explicit `types`, removed deprecated
      downlevelIteration/baseUrl; typescript-plugin pins explicit defaults —
      target ES2021 (the level ServiceNow supports; ES5 is a TS6 deprecation
      error), TS5's implied-module rule, emit-time suppression of the new
      "use strict" prologue, and Bundler instead of the removed node10
      resolution for Classic-implying configs — so plugin output stays
      deterministic across compiler majors). typescript 7.0.2 remains blocked by
      typescript-eslint's peer range `<6.1.0` and will be picked up when
      typescript-eslint widens it — tracked by normal Dependabot majors now that
      the `.github/dependabot.yml` ignore list has been removed.
- [x] **G17. Tests must not dirty the tracked tree** — DONE 2026-06-13: the
      culprit was commandsDownload.test.ts — downloadCommand calls the REAL
      generateScopeDocs(man), which resolves its outDir from process.cwd() and
      so rewrote packages/core/docs/scopes/x_test.md (cwd = packages/core under
      jest) with a fresh timestamp every run. Fixed by stubbing ../scopeDocs in
      that test (the test is about download orchestration, not doc generation).
